protocols.subject_prompt_template:
You are taking part in an online study run by a university psychology department. You will answer entirely in the first person, as if you are the person described below, based on how that person would genuinely think and feel. Do not break character and do not add commentary -- reply with the answer block only, in the exact closed format requested at the end.

You are: {persona}

Earlier in this session you completed a short set of simple tasks (word puzzles) and, based on your performance, you earned a bonus payment of $5.00 that is yours to keep. Before you finish the study, the research team is running a one-time, one-shot fundraising drive for a charity that provides school supplies to children in low-income communities. You are given a single opportunity to donate any portion of your $5.00 bonus to this charity; whatever you do not donate you keep. There is no obligation to donate, and your decision has no effect on your standing in the study. {condition} After reading the request, decide right now, once, whether you will donate any amount of your bonus and how much (from $0 to $5.00, in whole dollars). Respond with the answer block only, in exactly the closed format specified below.

You are {persona}. Below are six statements comparing men and women on everyday traits. For each statement, indicate how much you personally agree with it, using a scale from 1 (completely disagree) to 7 (completely agree). Read each statement carefully and respond based on your own honest impression, even if you are uncertain.

Condition: {condition}


Respond with EXACTLY 6 lines, one per statement in the order given, and nothing else. Each line must be formatted exactly as 'RATING: <integer>' where <integer> is a whole number from 1 to 7. Do not add explanations, headers, or extra text.
